  sw1/sw2 swing prices, and it returns `None` on `oppose`, `conflicted`,
  and `none`. That is not the audit fix (hand-verifiable swing prices on
  every 5m SMT status). Do not mark S11 done or merely "pending."
  **Deprioritized** for now per current direction — not scheduled for the
  confirmation-timing / session-window / SL / confluence-clock cleanup pass.
- Do **NOT** fix S4–S10 in v8.8 — they are Medium/Low severity and out of
  scope for this version per the audit's recommended sequence.

## FVG_AFTER_SMT stop-loss (intended; not an original S-item)

SL anchors to the most recent swing low (LONG) or swing high (SHORT) with a
timestamp **strictly before the FVG bar's timestamp**. Re-derive that lookup
fresh at the FVG bar — do not reuse a positional index comparison against
the swing-history snapshot from the outer scan bar. Full invariant:
`scanner-structural-correctness.mdc`.

After S1/S2/S3/S11 are fixed: re-run v8.8 on the existing Feb–Apr data and
review only the signals that changed relative to v8.7. Then freeze v8.8 before
running it once, blind, on unreviewed May–June data for the real out-of-sample
test. (S11 remaining incomplete does not block the structural-correctness
cleanup pass.)
